=== HINT 1: Allocate + set ===
g_tls_slot = TlsAlloc();
if (g_tls_slot == TLS_OUT_OF_INDEXES) { /* error */ }
TlsSetValue(g_tls_slot, (void*)(uintptr_t)tid);

=== HINT 2: Get + free ===
DWORD stored = (DWORD)(uintptr_t)TlsGetValue(g_tls_slot);
assert(stored == tid);
...in main, after all threads finish: TlsFree(g_tls_slot);

=== HINT 3 (KEY INSIGHT) ===
TlsGetValue returns the value SET BY THE CURRENT THREAD for that slot - each
thread has independent storage under the same slot index. Static alternative
(compiler extension): __declspec(thread) DWORD thread_id;. Dynamic TLS is
needed when the slot is not known at compile time (e.g. inside a DLL).
